                <pb facs="0170" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v23/pg123"/>

                <head>59. Evening Report Prepared for President Carter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d59-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1979-08-24T23:59:59-04:00"
                            notBefore="1979-08-21T00:00:00-04:00">undated</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">EVENING REPORT ITEMS</p>
                <p>[Omitted here is discussion of intelligence collection.]</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">August 20</hi>—Intelligence community has developed new
                    communication and photographic information on what appears to be a recent
                    exercise of a Soviet tank battalion in Cuba, which suggests that the Soviets
                    have the equivalent of a full brigade of 2,300 personnel on the island. (TS)</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">August 21</hi>—Three Soviet battalions were identified
                    as taking part in exercises August 17, 18, 19 and 20. Photos reveal more than 30
                    tanks and enough tents to accommodate 1,850 men. It thus seems clear that we are
                    dealing with at least one full-sized Soviet combat brigade. (TS)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
